  data:  # d421
    kind: work_item  # d421
    title: "Seven linkers still declare host languages they never read; the family WI-ditir closed on one instance of"  # d421
    status: todo_hard  # d421
    priority: 2  # d421
    parent:  # d421
    tags: []  # d421
    isbefore: []  # d421
    duplicate_of: []  # d421
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d421
    pr_ref:  # d421
    description: "RESIDUAL OF WI-ditir, which closed on its filed instance (database-query-linker,\nrepaired to depends_on=[[\"sql\"]]). The general claim that row made -- too-wide\ndepends_on clauses are invisible to falsification -- is still true of the tree\nand is NOT asserted resolved by that closure.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. depends_on is defined as \"the upstream analyzer pass IDs whose\noutput this linker structurally requires\". A clause is an inner-OR, so ANY one\nmember satisfies it. A clause that names languages the linker never reads is\ntherefore satisfiable on repositories where the linker cannot have read\nanything -- the FALSE-ALL-CLEAR direction. find_falsified_dependencies is\nbackward-looking and can only catch a clause that is too NARROW, so this class\nis invisible to the detector by construction and has to be found by reading.\n\nENUMERATED 2026-09-22 (declared language literals in conjunct #0 vs the glob\nconstants the module actually scans):\n\n  subprocess-linker       9 declared, scans **/*.py ONLY\n  orm-linker              8 declared, scans **/*.py ONLY\n  http-linker            13 declared, scans 9\n  message-queue-linker    9 declared, scans 4 -- and reads NO ctx.symbols\n  grpc-linker            12 declared, scans 6 (incl. .proto -- a real dependency)\n  event-sourcing-linker   6 declared, scans 5\n  graphql-resolver-linker 6 declared, scans 3 (incl. graphql -- a real dependency)\n  crypto-flow-linker     10 declared, 0 glob constants -- locates files by some\n                            other route; needs individual reading before any verdict\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT A SWEEP, and must not become one. database-query-linker was the\nclean specimen: it consumes NO pass output on the query side, taking\nctx.repo_root and re-reading from disk, so deleting the conjunct was\nunambiguous. Most of the linkers above DO read ctx.symbols, so some part of\ntheir host-language clause may name a real producer. Each needs its own\nverification of what it actually consumes. Applying one rule to all eight is\nthe same too-wide reasoning the family is about.\n\nTHE SHAPE OF EACH REPAIR, per the WI-dinum precedent shipped for graphql-linker\nand now database-query-linker: name the pass that can supply the edge\nDESTINATION, not the language where the source pattern was found.\n\nALSO OPEN, and larger: recording a linker's SCAN CAPABILITY somewhere honest.\nWI-ditir proposed `activation`, but LinkerActivation has only always /\nframeworks / language_pairs -- no file-shape field. Adding one is a core\ndataclass change carrying ADR-0024 axis-declaration obligations, so it is its\nown decision, not a rider on any of the eight repairs above.\n\nSTARTING POINT: message-queue-linker is the strongest candidate for the next\nclean specimen -- 9 declared languages and no ctx.symbols read at all, which is\ndatabase-query-linker's exact shape."  # d421
    fields: {}  # d421
- op: discuss  # 8dba
  at: '2026-09-22T08:14:11Z'  # 8dba
  by: agent  # 8dba
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8dba
  clock: 2  # 8dba
  nonce: 8dba  # 8dba
  message: "PARTIAL: 2 of 8 repaired, merged to dev. This row stays open for the other six.\n\nDONE:\n  graphql-resolver-linker  [5 host languages + graphql] -> [['graphql','graphql-sdl-linker']]\n      Its only read of pass output is _get_graphql_schema_symbols, filtering\n      ctx.symbols on language=='graphql' and kind in (type,field,interface).\n      The resolver side is read off disk. Same pair WI-dinum settled for the\n      sibling graphql-linker, and graphql-sdl-linker is included because it\n      emits the kind='field' records the GraphQL analyzer never has.\n  message-queue-linker     [9 host languages] -> []\n      link_message_queues(root: Path) consumes NOTHING and mints BOTH ENDS of\n      every edge, so no pass supplies source or destination.\n\nA RATIFIED CRITERION HAD TO BE AMENDED, and the owner ruled it rather than me.\nWI-dilab's closure criterion (INV-hujog's gate) requires every Bridge/Framework/\nProtocol linker to declare a NON-EMPTY depends_on, and message-queue-linker is\na Protocol linker. Its premise -- that such a linker always reads some\nanalyzer's output -- is false for a self-scanner. Forcing a non-empty clause\ndoes not make the declaration true; it makes it a list of passes the linker\nnever reads, which is the defect this family is about.\n\nThe amendment is narrow and POSITIVE: an empty clause is allowed only when the\nmodule docstring states, in a fixed phrase the gate greps for, why it is empty.\nSilence plus an empty clause is STILL an offence -- silence is indistinguishable\nfrom having forgotten to declare, which is what the criterion exists to catch.\nTwo further tests keep it honest: one asserts the branch is actually exercised\n(a dead allowance should be deleted, not carried), one asserts an undeclared\nempty clause still trips the gate.\n\nSTILL OPEN, and why each is not a sweep -- ALL SIX genuinely read ctx.symbols,\nunlike the two above, so part of each clause may name a real producer:\n  http-linker            13 declared, scans 9 globs\n  grpc-linker            12 declared, scans 6 -- also reads ctx.EDGES\n  crypto-flow-linker     10 declared, 0 glob constants (finds files another way)\n  subprocess-linker       9 declared, scans **/*.py ONLY\n  orm-linker              8 declared, scans **/*.py ONLY\n  event-sourcing-linker   6 declared, scans 5\n\nhttp-linker is the hardest and should NOT be guessed: it consumes route\nsymbols, and route_of() accepts BOTH an analyzer-written framework_role=='route'\nmarker AND a framework-YAML concept=='route' entry. So its producer set is not\nanalyzer-only and cannot be derived by the _pass_ids_writing AST scan alone.\n\nsubprocess-linker and orm-linker are the next cleanest: each declares 8-9\nlanguages while scanning only **/*.py, so the gap is largest and the symbol\nconsumption is narrow enough to enumerate."  # 8dba
