- op: discuss  # 1246
  at: '2026-09-22T23:13:45Z'  # 1246
  by: agent  # 1246
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1246
  clock: 4  # 1246
  nonce: '1246'  # 1246
  message: "DONE: the last six repaired, merged (1ce482aa6b). Each clause was derived by reading what the linker consumes:\n  http-linker -> the 15 host analyzers that can supply a path-bearing route record. Drops elm (client-scan only); adds play-routes, clojure, groovy.\n  crypto-flow-linker -> [[javascript, rust, rust_analyzer]]. Its entire file list is symbols of those languages.\n  subprocess-linker -> [[python, scip_python]]; orm-linker -> [[python]].\n  event-sourcing-linker, grpc-linker -> [] under the WI-dilab fixed docstring phrase.\nEVIDENCE, production-path tests on get_default_catalog(): test_depends_on_producer_sets.py now DERIVES the http, crypto-flow, subprocess and orm producer sets from the analyzers' source, with a one-directional cover gate plus an exact pin. All 9 new tests were red before the change. The catalog gates (literals resolve, empty-clause phrase, conjunct floor) pass. The CLI catalog view does not expose depends_on, so there is no CLI-level repro to re-run.\nAll 8 of the family's linkers are now repaired (2 in the earlier partial, 6 here). The row's other open question, recording a linker's SCAN CAPABILITY honestly (a file-shape field on LinkerActivation), is NOT done. It is a core dataclass change with ADR-0024 axis obligations, and it stays its own decision.\nFILED from the derivation: WI-gopok (orm/subprocess destination lookups are not language-filtered)."  # 1246
